eia930_demand_growth rows as the page reads them (table_rows.csv, 16 November 2026): years 2019 to 2026; last whole year 2025

== line 1: California's growth with the batteries' charging (the table's row) and without (a second row)
June to December 2025: demand +2.81 percent on the same months of 2019 (26,383 to 27,124 MW, +741 MW); the charging 1,690 MW; demand less the charging -3.60 percent; CAISO's own demand -3.25 percent; retail sales -2.28 percent; the charging is 228 percent of the growth
January to August 2026: demand +10.75 percent on the same months of 2019 (24,282 to 26,893 MW, +2,611 MW); the charging 2,114 MW; demand less the charging +2.05 percent; CAISO's own demand +2.13 percent; retail sales -2.90 percent; the charging is 81 percent of the growth
EIA's demand less CAISO's own is the charging to within 300 MW in 14 of the 16 months held (2025-06 to 2026-09)
the page's headline for CAISO (2025 on 2019, the whole year): +4.45 percent. A second row for the whole year needs the charging of January to May 2025, which CAISO's own data on this machine does not hold (iso:caiso_own starts in June 2025): the whole-year figure without the charging is not computed

